+# Q3 2026 Operating Brief
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Q3 was a solid quarter financially, with revenue of $720,000 against spend of
+$464,000, leaving an operating surplus of $256,000. Support held up well,
+closing the large majority of the quarter's tickets. The security team kept
+pace with incident volume, resolving 95.0% of detected incidents. The Q4
+delivery plan is on track, with a launch date in late October pending
+confirmation (see Notes). Overall the business is healthy, with a few
+data-quality items below that leadership should be aware of.
+
+## Key figures
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |
+| Q3 spend | $464,000 |
+| Operating surplus | $256,000 |
+| Support close rate | 93.7% |
+| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |
+| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |
+
+## Notes
+
+Three figures quoted directly in the source packets did not match the
+underlying data and were recalculated for this brief; leadership should be
+aware these headline numbers have been corrected:
+
+- **Q3 spend**: the finance packet's summary line states $463,250, but the
+  itemized spend categories (payroll, infrastructure, contractors,
+  facilities) sum to $464,000. The corrected figure is used above, which
+  also shifts the operating surplus to $256,000 (vs. an implied $256,750).
+- **Support close rate**: the support packet's dashboard label states 96.4%,
+  but 1,171 closed of 1,250 opened tickets computes to 93.7%.
+- **Launch date**: the delivery packet's summary states 2026-10-22, but
+  walking the phase durations (Discovery 3d, Build 6d, QA 4d, Release 1d)
+  from the 2026-10-05 start date — accounting for weekends and the
+  2026-10-12 company holiday, and starting each phase on the next business
+  day after the prior phase ends — lands on 2026-10-23, one business day
+  later than reported.
+
+No issues to escalate from the security packet; the 95.0% resolution rate
+(76 of 80 incidents) matches the underlying counts.
